  "question": {
    "text": "A coil of inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> having negligible resistance is connected to a source of supply whose voltage is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi></math> volt. (where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in second). If the voltage is applied when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, then the energy stored in the coil after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>,",
    "image": null
